{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p3-b57fa8ae","text":"The dropzone markup looks normal (full-width label). The screenshot strip is likely the `.thumbs` empty? No, dashed line is dropzone. Why would it be a narrow vertical strip at the left with a weird curve? In the screenshot, the strip is under the "Property photos" heading, about 78px wide and 160px tall, with rounded dashed border; to its right is empty space. That suggests the dropzone is being rendered inside a **flex/grid container that gives it width ~80px** and its content wrapped invisibly? But the title/hint text isn't visible inside the strip. Maybe the strip isn't the dropzone but the **image counter bar**? It has a dashed border? The counter has `.counter` block: `flex: 1 1 260px` with a bar. Hmm, the strip's top aligns with heading, bottom aligns with "6 photos" — that's the full photos panel content height. So the dashed strip spans from heading to the counter.

Could this be Chrome's **file input** rendering? `.dropzone input { display:none }` so no.

Maybe it's the `<label class="dropzone">` collapsed because of CSS `columns`? No.

Wait, the screenshot is tiny (366x310) and seems to be a clipped close-up. The dashed line with rounded corners might be the *left edge of the dropzone* whose rest extends off-image to the right; the screenshot may be cropped. "weird sidelined dotted line" — perhaps the user sees the dropzone border as dashed on the left only because the rest is out of view? The image shows the dashed border with a curve at ~y=170 turning right and stopping — like the border of the dropzone at a column width of ~78px with a weird extra curve. Hmm.

Actually look closer: the dashed rectangle starts at x≈30, width≈50, from y≈50 to y≈290. At y≈170 there's a horizontal dashed segment going right ~40px then curving down? It looks like two nested dashed rectangles overlapping—maybe the dropzone and the empty-state both dashed, but empty-state is below, not overlapping.

Could it be the `.counter__bar` rendered vertically? No dashed.

Let me reproduce in the browser at a narrow viewport and screenshot. Need to open index page, go to Photos tab, and set viewport narrow (e.g., 390px) to see mobile layout. The user's screenshot width 366 suggests mobile/narrow preview. Use preview_resize 390x800, navigate, click Photos tab, screenshot. We'll see.

