{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p11-b57fa8ae","text":"Now I see it clearly! The dashed border is rendering **only along the left and top of the text**, like a vertical dashed line behind the heading and around the dropzone, but the dropzone's background/padding seems collapsed? Actually the dropzone is the area containing "Drop photos here..." with dashed border visible only on the left side, and a vertical dashed line running up through the heading paragraph. The right border is off-screen? No, the sheet ends at x~447; the dashed line at x≈55 extends from y≈727 to 1050. The dropzone's full width border is missing except the left edge.

Why? The `.dropzone` is a `<label>` with `display` default inline! A `<label>` is inline by default. With border/padding and block children, it produces weird fragmented borders — inline boxes broken across lines render borders oddly (left border only at line starts, top border around first line, etc.). Exactly: it's an inline label, so its border wraps line boxes. At wide widths, the content stayed one line? The title/hint are block divs inside an inline label → anonymous block boxes → border fragments. That's the bug.

Fix: `.dropzone { display: block; }` (or flex column). That should render the full dashed rounded box.

Also mobile header issues visible: Freebuff badge overlaps brand; page title huge. But that's the Freebuff overlay, not our app. Horizontal scrollbar in tablist is intentional (overflow-x auto), though it extends beyond sheet? Fine.

Now the other requests:

2. AI settings tab redundant: remove the tab from wizard. Need to edit:
- templates/index.html: remove tab button for ai, renumber progress 6 and result 7 => 5 and 6; remove panel-ai section (or keep provider summary? remove).
- app.js: TABS array, LAST_FORM_TAB, boot etc. Search "ai" tab references.
- Any link "go-to-settings" from panel? Remove.
- update app copy "seven-step" in README, but user-facing docs can be updated. They asked deployable too; docs overhaul.

3. Developer copy:
- Settings sidebar left section: inspect settings.html. Replace "LOCAL ONLY" panel, "prototype" and technical notes with user-facing setup guidance.
- Footer in base.html: remove "Runs on this computer only..." and "local prototype". Replace with concise product footer: "Your media and API keys stay on your server." plus "Background music must be licensed..." maybe keep rights notice (user-relevant, not dev). User said "footer that says run in localhost and everything" — remove localhost mention.
- Remove "Template mode" badge? It's useful. Keep.
- Header topbar status "AI script ready" showing erroneously (no key) — need to check. Probably because settings state saved? Let's inspect `/api/settings` secrets — gemini maybe still configured from the fake test? We removed via UI, but the second save (clear-field-test) was followed by Remove click; status showed "No key saved". Yet page says "AI script ready" (has_llm_key true). Maybe the page is stale from before remove; it was loaded at ?, and we removed key after. The page reloaded? We navigated root ?v=5 after remove, so should reflect. Check settings store. Maybe remove deleted only UI key but env? No. Let me check `has_llm_key` in boot.

Also "deployable" work: need to decide scope. Let's inspect settings.html to see left section and layout.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
